<title>GERMANY: Bayer says may pay higher 1996 dividend.</title>
<headline>Bayer says may pay higher 1996 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>LEVERKUSEN, Germany 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals and drugs group Bayer AG said on Tuesday it might pay a higher dividend for 1996.</p>
<p>Chief executive Manfred Schneider told a news conference that a higher payout was possible if the company achieved its goals for 1996 results.</p>
<p>Bayer earlier said it expected to post a 10 percent rise in operating income for 1996 after its nine-month pre-tax profit rose 12 percent to 3.7 billion marks.</p>
<p>The company paid a 1995 dividend of 15 marks.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
